WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Why pick up the phone just after putting it down?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Familiar contexts can cue familiar actions.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
A 2010 study tracked everyday habit formation.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
People repeated chosen actions in stable contexts.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Automaticity developed at different rates.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Look at the cue and the next action together.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
What is easiest to reach can be easiest to start.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
A repeated route can grow more familiar.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
The path is a metaphor for context and action.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
No fixed number of days guarantees a habit.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
One missed attempt need not define everything.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Complex difficulties may need broader support.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Open the book. Reduce the work before starting.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Try two minutes and observe the arrangement.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Adjust the environment and allow rest.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Look for a cue before making a global judgment.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Make a useful small action easier.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Bring the next beginning a little closer.
